{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch48LKi4gDG5jQcZSasUS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the spelling but haven't committed, because a single commit would only get one of the three months through the nightly import.\n\n**The fix:** there was one `wholsale` in each of the September, October and November files, and all three now say `wholesale`. No other file had the misspelling. `scripts/check.sh` passed, and this time that means something because all three files are 2025, which is the year it checks. The changes are sitting uncommitted in the working tree.\n\n**The problem with one commit:** the README says the nightly import \"reloads, for each new commit, only the data file of the month its message starts with, so a commit that touches several months loads only that one.\" `check.sh` prints the same warning. A single commit starting with `2025-09` would reload September, and the import would keep the old misspelling for October and November.\n\nHow would you like to go ahead?\n1. **Three commits** (`2025-09: fix wholesale spelling`, then the same for `2025-10` and `2025-11`), so each month gets reloaded. This is what I'd suggest.\n2. **One commit anyway,** if the import doesn't matter here or you'll reload October and November another way."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":586,"cache_read_input_tokens":27051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":586},"output_tokens":357,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-100>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T05:02:22.658Z","request_id":"req_011Ch48LKVuJA18MyqWudm7m"}
